  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Total federal contract obligations to Massachusetts are $14.6B for FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer in the state, obligating $11.3B. Obligations are down 24.4% year over year. The state has 81,697 awards so far, with an average award size of $179K. Recent fiscal-year trends show obligations of $24.2B in FY21, $17.9B in FY22, $18.3B in FY23, $17.8B in FY24, $19.3B in FY25, and $14.6B in FY26 to date. The top industries by obligations include Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $3B and Engineering Services at $1.7B. Major vendors with notable obligations include RAYTHEON COMPANY at $3.4B, GENERAL ELECTRIC COMPANY at $1.3B, and MASSACHUSETTS INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY at $1B. This snapshot covers contract obligations only and reflects a fiscal-year-to-date total that is partial for the current year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What is the current scale and recent trend in federal contracting for Massachusetts?",
        "body": "Total federal contract obligations to Massachusetts are $14.6B for FY2026 to date. Obligations are down 24.4% year over year. The state has 81,697 awards so far and the average award size is $179K. Historical obligations by fiscal year are $24.2B in FY21, $17.9B in FY22, $18.3B in FY23, $17.8B in FY24, and $19.3B in FY25."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries account for the largest share of federal obligations in Massachusetts?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $11.3B in Massachusetts for FY2026 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs, Department of Transportation, and Department of Health and Human Services follow with $836M, $722M, and $505M respectively. The largest industries by obligations are Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $3B and Engineering Services at $1.7B. Other sizable industry categories include Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $1.4B and Aircraft Engine and Engine Parts Manufacturing at $1.2B."
      }
    ]
